Package: cbamm
Type: Package
Title: Ultimate Meta-Analysis: Component NMA, Advanced Heterogeneity, ML, Bayesian, Living Reviews
Version: 2.4.0
Authors@R: person("Mahmood", "Ahmad", email = "mahmood.ahmad2@nhs.net",
                        role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: The most comprehensive and cutting-edge meta-analysis system available,
    implementing state-of-the-art methods from top statistical journals (Statistics in
    Medicine, Research Synthesis Methods, Biometrics, BMC Medical Research Methodology).
    NEW in v2.4.0: Component network meta-analysis (CNMA) for multicomponent interventions
    with additive and interaction models; advanced meta-regression with restricted cubic
    splines and penalized regression (LASSO/Ridge/Elastic Net) for high-dimensional
    moderators; 8 advanced heterogeneity estimators (Paule-Mandel, Sidik-Jonkman, Empirical
    Bayes, ML, REML, Hunter-Schmidt, Hedges) with Hartung-Knapp-Sidik-Jonkman small-sample
    adjustment and prediction intervals; cross-design synthesis for combining RCTs with
    observational studies; prevalence/proportion meta-analysis with 5 variance-stabilizing
    transformations (logit, arcsine, Freeman-Tukey). PREVIOUS: Traditional methods (DL, REML,
    Bayesian MCMC), network meta-analysis with SUCRA rankings, multivariate MA for correlated
    outcomes, dose-response with splines, revolutionary ML (RF, XGBoost, SVM, neural networks),
    AI intelligence (Gemini, Ollama), living systematic reviews (PubMed, Crossref, OpenAlex),
    advanced publication bias (PET-PEESE, selection models, p-curve, p-uniform, limit MA),
    automated PRISMA manuscripts, comprehensive sensitivity analysis (15+ methods). Optimized
    with parallel processing. Over 25,000 lines of production code implementing 50+
    meta-analytic methods.
